      },
      {
        "text": "Historical examples of such fraud include tobacco industry-funded scientists creating doubt about smoking risks.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Similar patterns exist in debates over environmental pollutants and public health.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "A new kind of predatory behavior has emerged in the current scientific landscape.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "The distinction between genuine, legitimate, and fake science is clear enough to be practically useful.",
